Psiring: change-ringing program for the Psion Series 3

MENUS

METHOD

- DISPLAY (Psion-D: show method, calling, tenor, your bell selection, whether blueline will be displayed in simulator

- SELECT (Psion-S):  Method selection - enter search string and then accept or reject found matches

- EXIT (Psion-X):  leave the program (after Yes/No confirmation dialog)

DISPLAY

- TABLE (Psion-T): display lead in form of table of numbers. Pick out path of various bells by entering the number. Show callings by entering call letters p(lain), b(ob), or s(ingle).

- BLUE LINE (Psion-B): display blue line with starts. Scroll l/r if necessary.

- LEAD (Psion-L): show two leads (line diagrams); change to bob or single (b or s).

- LEAD HEADS (Psion-H): show lead heads after lead of P(lain), B(ob), or S(ingle).

RING

- CALL (Psion-C): display and alter calling.

- AUTO (Psion-A): starts automatic simulation.

- MANUAL (Psion-M): starts simulation with your bell (if selected) manually operated by H(and) and B(ack) keys.

SYSTEM

- MENU ON/OFF (Psion-O): toggle automatic menu display on/off.

- HELP (Psion-E): display all entries in Ringhelp file. Scroll left/right through entries or up/down.

- FILE PATH (Psion-F): display or set path for data files.
